Port DeepFilterNet libDF (Rikorose/DeepFilterNet d375b2d) to tract 0.23.8 and fix quality/robustness.
Apply with `git apply` on top of that commit (native/deepfilter/build.sh does this), together with
the pinned native/deepfilter/Cargo.lock.

  * tract-{core,onnx,pulse,hir} ^0.21.4 -> =0.23.8; API port in libDF/src/tract.rs (ndarray is
    tract_core::ndarray = 0.17, plain tensor views, TValue = Arc<Tensor>, SimpleState::new(&plan),
    symbols, with_outputs_by_name).
  * features `capi` and `wasm` no longer force `default-model` (model passed at runtime);
    `wasm` also enables getrandom 0.4's browser backend (pulled in by tract 0.23).
  * capi.rs: df_create defaults to always-on stages; new df_create_with_params and df_last_error;
    df_create* return NULL instead of panicking; df_process_frame catches panics.
    New cargo profile `release-capi` (release-lto with panic=unwind) so that works.
  * wasm.rs: df_create always-on stages; new df_create_with_params, df_process_frames (batch),
    df_free; errors are thrown as JS errors; console_error_panic_hook installed.

